 Persistence

Persistence is the source of truth.

It contains products, customers, promotions, coupons, prices, inventory, and shipping rules.

Cartique never owns this data.

It only receives it.

 Commerce Model

The commerce model is a set of immutable objects.


Sellable
Variant
Customer
Place
Context
Promotion
Coupon


These objects are pure data.

They contain no behavior.

They contain no logic.

They are simply facts.

 Resolution Engine

The resolution engine is a deterministic compiler.

It receives commercial facts and produces commercial truth.


Input:  Sellable, Customer, Configuration, Place, Contexts
Process: Variant → Pricing → Promotion → Tax → Shipping
Output: CommercialDecision


 Commercial Decision

The commercial decision is an immutable object.


items
adjustments
totals
journal
diagnostics


It is the commercial truth.

It is explainable.

It is auditable.

It is repeatable.



 The Principles

 Principle 1: Database is the Source of Truth

Cartique never owns commerce data.

It computes commerce decisions.

The kernel never creates, persists, or queries data.

 Principle 2: Commerce Objects are Immutable

Everything entering the kernel becomes immutable.

No resolver mutates anything.

Every resolver returns a new state.

 Principle 3: Kernel Never Talks To Database

No Prisma.

No SQL.

No fetch().

No HTTP.

No Redis.

Pure computation only.

 Principle 4: Resolvers are Deterministic

Given the same inputs, every resolver produces the same output.

No randomness.

No clocks.

No network calls.

No hidden state.

 Principle 5: If It's Stored → Persistence. If It's Derived → Kernel.

This single rule keeps responsibilities clear and prevents business logic from leaking.



 The Resolvers

Each resolver answers exactly one question.


VariantResolver    → Which variant?
PricingResolver    → What price?
PromotionResolver  → What adjustments apply?
TaxResolver        → What tax applies?
ShippingResolver   → What shipping applies?


No resolver thinks.

No resolver knows about other resolvers.

No resolver mutates state.

No resolver is special.

They are all just functions.

They receive state.

They return patches.

The engine composes them.



 The Output

The output is a CommercialDecision.


CommercialDecision
├── items (what was purchased)
├── adjustments (what changed the price)
├── totals (subtotal, tax, shipping, total)
├── journal (why every decision was made)
└── diagnostics (errors, warnings, notices)


It is immutable.

It is explainable.

It is auditable.

It is repeatable.



 The Extension Model

New resolvers can be added without changing the kernel.


InventoryResolver    → Is stock available?
EligibilityResolver  → Is customer eligible?
CompositionResolver  → What is included?
FulfillmentResolver  → How is it fulfilled?


New capabilities can be added to Sellable without changing the kernel.


requiresInventory
requiresShipping
requiresFulfillment


New adapters can be added without changing the kernel.


REST API
Prisma
Shopify
Commerce Layer
Medusa


The kernel stays small.

The capabilities grow.



 The Future

Cartique is not finished.

It will never be finished.

Commerce evolves.

Cartique evolves with it.

But the core remains stable.


Core
├── Value Objects
├── Commerce Model
├── Resolution Engine
├── Commercial Decision
└── Resolver Contract


These never change.

Everything else is an enhancement.



 The Belief

Cartique is a belief.

A belief that commerce can be modeled through a small set of timeless primitives.

A belief that complexity should be achieved through composition, not accumulation.

A belief that truth should be computed, not stored.

A belief that intent should be portable.

A belief that history should be permanent.

A belief that the kernel should be stable while the ecosystem evolves.



 The One Sentence

> Cartique is a deterministic commerce decision engine that transforms a sellable, customer, configuration, place, and context into an immutable commercial decision.



